# Queues and Outbox

## Patterns
- Transactional outbox → RabbitMQ topic exchanges / routing keys in `libs/queue`
- Workers ack on success; nack without requeue on failure; use DLQ helpers intentionally
- Prefetch defaults to 1 — keep handlers short and idempotent

## Rules
- Every cross-service side effect goes through outbox in the same DB transaction as the write
- Consumers must be idempotent (dedupe by event id / business key)
- On poison messages: mark failed + DLQ; do not infinite-retry silently
- Version event payloads; avoid breaking consumers without dual-read
- Do not publish directly from request handlers when an outbox path exists
- When adding workers, update `scripts/docker/workloads.manifest.json` and regenerate compose/k3s — keep image CI in sync
